  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality carries useful signal for this task at all. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) establishes the image-only baseline under the same singleprofile, no-aggregation simplicity as config_001, enabling a direct modality comparison. If image accuracy substantially exceeds 48.5%, the search should pivot toward multimodal fusion and image-encoder selection; if it falls well below, RNA-focused improvements (multiprofile, learned encoders) become the priority. This single experiment resolves the highest-level design question—whether to invest in the image branch—before committing budget to more granular choices like aggregation, fusion strategy, or encoder variants, making it the most information-efficient next step."
}

